# Diagram quality checklist

## Model

- [ ] Every node has a reason to exist.
- [ ] Every edge is directional only when direction is meaningful.
- [ ] Ownership and external boundaries are visible.
- [ ] Inferred or unknown relationships are labeled rather than implied as facts.
- [ ] The diagram is smaller than the comprehension problem it solves.

## Artifact

- [ ] SVG/HTML parses and opens without remote assets or JavaScript requirements.
- [ ] Connectors are behind nodes and do not cross labels unnecessarily.
- [ ] Text remains legible at the intended viewport and on a narrow viewport.
- [ ] Title, description, alt text, and non-color cues are present.
- [ ] Source and rendered output are reviewed together.

## Evidence

- [ ] Scope and source of truth are linked from nearby documentation.
- [ ] Each claim maps to repository, configuration, deployment, or runtime evidence.
- [ ] Tool availability and fallback are recorded.
- [ ] Owner and update trigger are recorded.
- [ ] Unknown consumer or runtime behavior keeps the verdict conditional.
